  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ball is dropped from a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the coefficient of restitution for the collision between ball and floor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, after hitting the floor, the ball rebounds to a height of ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo></math>height after the collision,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo></math>height before the collision and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo></math>coefficient of restitution.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
